    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me verify the full change is consistent by confirming the audit log showed the expected behavior (`membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27`, `registrationDate=2026-10-05`) \u2014 a registration on 5 Oct 2026 correctly falls in fiscal year 2027 (FY27), and the membership number's year segment now uses `M27`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved all date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, labeled by its ending year so e.g. a 5 Oct 2026 registration \u2192 FY27).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`**\n   - Added `public static int fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 the single source of truth: months \u2265 July roll into the next year's fiscal year.\n   - Added read-only `getFiscalYear()` returning `FY<YY>` from the (already business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`; `null` when no registration date, so the field is simply omitted.\n   - Replaced `hasTenureOver365Days()` with `hasTenureOverOneFiscalYear()` \u2014 the 3 tenure points now trigger when at least one fiscal year has elapsed (`fiscalYearOf(now) - fiscalYearOf(registrationDate) >= 1`) instead of a 365-day window.\n   - Dropped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import; added `Month`.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 `generateMembershipNumber` now uses `Owner.fiscalYearOf(registrationDate) % 100` for the `-M<YY>` segment instead of the raw calendar year.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped the new `fiscalYear` field onto `OwnerDto`.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` schema property (so the generated DTO exposes it) and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures), including the new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` acceptance test asserting the response carries a `FY\\d{2}` fiscal year.\n\nNote: these files aren't under version control (not a git repo), so I've made the edits in place without committing.",
