    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\nKey points I checked:\n\n- **Logic placed in the right unit.** The fiscal-year rule (the \"starts 1 July\" threshold) is captured once in `Owner.fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` and reused by both `Owner.getFiscalYear()` / `hasTenureOverOneFiscalYear()` and `ClinicServiceImpl.generateMembershipNumber`. No duplication of the July cutoff across the model and service \u2014 the service now calls the shared helper instead of re-deriving the year segment.\n\n- **Owner is the natural home.** Owner already owns the family of registration-date-derived, `@Transient` read-only values (`getAgeBand`, `getMembershipPoints`, `getCheckDigit`, etc.), so `getFiscalYear()` sits right alongside its peers, and the rename `hasTenureOver365Days \u2192 hasTenureOverOneFiscalYear` keeps the private helper consistent with the new semantics. Nothing is becoming a catch-all.\n\n- **Mapper follows the established pattern.** `@Mapping(target = \"fiscalYear\", expression = \"java(owner.getFiscalYear())\")` mirrors the existing direct-getter delegation used for `salutation` (line 27), so no gratuitous `toFiscalYear` helper is warranted.\n\n- **\"Business-day-adjusted\" wording is coherent.** `registrationDate` is stored already business-day-adjusted at create time (`ClinicServiceImpl` line 263\u2013265 via `toBusinessDay`), so the javadoc/openapi phrasing about the \"business-day-adjusted registrationDate\" is accurate and consistent across the model, service, and `openapi.yml`.\n\n- **Docs/examples updated in lockstep** (openapi `fiscalYear` schema added, membership-number and membership-points descriptions and examples updated to the fiscal-year basis).\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this natural.",
